course: dictionary
lesson: 310
title: Ancestors and where words come from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ancestor is someone your family came from who lived long ago, before your grandparents. In «Bon Odori is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival, which honours the spirits of ancestors», the words «honours» and «spirits» are clues. People honour ancestors, so ancestors must be people from long ago who matter to a family.
explain: The word also works for animals, plants, machines and ideas. The wolf is an ancestor of the dog, meaning the dog developed from an older kind of wolf-like animal. Birds have dinosaur ancestors, so a bird is a later form of an older animal. When you meet a word that could mean more than one thing, read the sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: Sentences often hint at a meaning without stating it. «Languages that grew from the same ancestor form a family» tells you that an ancestor is the starting point of something that later branched out. English and Hindi share one, which is why some words look alike in both. Always ask: what does this word do in the sentence?
fact: An ancestor is a person in your family who lived long ago, before your grandparents.
fact: An ancestor of an animal or plant is an older kind it developed from. The wolf is an ancestor of the dog.
fact: An ancestor of a machine or idea is an earlier form of it.
fact: Languages that grew from the same ancestor form a family, such as the Indo-European family.
fact: Many cultures honour their ancestors, such as the Māori idea of whakapapa.
exercise: «Bon Odori is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival, which honours the spirits of ancestors.» What does ancestors mean in this sentence? | Summer weather | Animals that live in the wild | Dances in a big circle | *People from long ago in a family
exercise: «The wolf is an ancestor of the dog.» What does ancestor mean here? | A dog that is very old and sleepy | *An older kind of animal that the dog developed from | A dog's bowl | A dog that lives in a house
exercise: «Birds have dinosaur ancestors.» Which kind of animal is the ancestor of birds? | Horses | Penguins | Fish | *Dinosaurs
test: Mum says, «Our ancestors came from Ireland.» What does ancestors mean? | Friends who visit at Christmas | *People in our family who lived long ago | Our neighbours next door | Brothers and sisters
test: Two cousins share a common ancestor. What does common ancestor mean? | A house they both own | *A family member from long ago whom both cousins come from | A new pet they both like | A cousin who lives with them
exam: The old telephone with a wire is an ancestor of the mobile phone. What does ancestor mean here? | *An earlier form of the machine that the newer one developed from | A phone that is broken | A phone that has no battery | A phone sold in a shop
